				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13431442/scp-5950#post-4689524</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2020 23:25:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>ManyMeats</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2104082</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>The two instances (designated SCP-5950-1 and SCP-5950-2) acted as a mating pair, though no offspring were ever produced.</p> </blockquote> <p>Thanks for not going there.</p> <p>This was short and weird, and overall worth a +1. I want to say &quot;but just barely&quot; although that's not quite right. I mean to give full credit that this is definitely worth a +1 in a vacuum, but the clarification I hope to make is that there's only barely enough here for this to feel like a full piece to me. Credit where credit is due!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
